HTTP IPv6 source binding for NICo boot

Core identifies HTTP clients by their registered address, such as a DHCPv6
lease or an inferred EUI-64 SLAAC address.  Automatic source selection can
otherwise use an address Core does not recognize.  The optional `http-source6`
setting binds HTTP and HTTPS connections to an address and interface; the
embedded script decides when to set or clear it.

Configured payload URLs may use hostnames, so resolution must return IPv6
destinations even when the DNS server is IPv4.  Each connection keeps its
binding, including when it is reused from the HTTP connection pool.

Manual self-test: apply the repository's iPXE patches to an isolated iPXE
tree and copy `pxe/ipxe/local/*.h` into its `src/config/local/` directory.
From that tree's `src/` directory, run:

    make -j8 bin-x86_64-linux/tests.linux DEBUG=http_source_test
    ./bin-x86_64-linux/tests.linux

